    <div class="container home-section__inner">
      <div class="home-head">
        <div class="home-eyebrow home-eyebrow--section">Operations</div>
        <h2>Pools that scale with people, not noise.</h2>
        <p>Assignment is per session and atomic in Redis. A spare pool is kept ready, another is provisioned as soon as a session has to borrow one, and idle pools are recycled after thirty minutes. Resource budgets stop growth before the host runs short.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="home-split">
        <div class="home-copy">
          <ul class="home-points" style="margin-top: 0;">
            <li><Icon name="box" class="w-4 h-4" /><span><strong>Exclusive by default.</strong> A session gets its own shop and database pair; the mapping is stored with a 24-hour TTL.</span></li>
            <li><Icon name="zap" class="w-4 h-4" /><span><strong>Spare provisioning.</strong> Every assignment queues a wake-up, so the next visitor usually finds a warm pool.</span></li>
            <li><Icon name="gauge" class="w-4 h-4" /><span><strong>Bounded growth.</strong> <code>POOL_MAX</code>, memory, CPU, load and disk guards cap the fleet; beyond that sessions share pools round-robin.</span></li>
            <li><Icon name="clock" class="w-4 h-4" /><span><strong>Scale down.</strong> Idle pools above the spare count are removed and their users reassigned on return.</span></li>
            <li><Icon name="archive" class="w-4 h-4" /><span><strong>Content sync.</strong> Production pages, posts and products are mirrored into every pool every five minutes by default.</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p style="margin-top: 1.35rem;">
            <a href="/docs/engine">Explore the honeypot engine <Icon name="arrow" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" style="display: inline-block; vertical-align: -2px;" /></a>
